msgctxt "bark 0419:28A6"
msgid "Funny that Torwin should lose it there. He was very proud of it, said it meant the world to him. You know, I think it should be returned to his mother. I'm sure she would appreciate this memento of her son. "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "the monastery " or "the woods "
msgctxt "ask 0419"
msgid "I don't wish to return it. "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "Windy Point "
msgctxt "bark 0419:2A25"
msgid "Oh dear. In his haste to end his life, he must have lost it. It is a terrible tragedy, you know. He was very proud of that ring and I'm sure he would want his mother to have it. Perhaps you should take it to her. "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "I will return it. "
#. answer compared by the conversation code
msgctxt "ask 0419"
msgid "I will return it. "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "I will return it. "
msgctxt "bark 0419:2B9C"
msgid "That is a good thing. His mother's name is Rhian and she lives in Tenebrae. She is a weaver and, since the death of her husband, has taken over the running of the shop. Thank you for this good deed. "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "I don't wish to return it. "
msgctxt "bark 0419:2CDE"
msgid "What? That is a cruel and selfish thing to say! You must return it. You were the last one to see her son alive! I can not believe you would turn your back on someone like this! "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "I don't wish to return it. "
msgctxt "ask 0419"
msgid "I said I would not! "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "I said I would not! "
msgctxt "bark 0419:2DC0"
msgid "Have you learned nothing during your stay here?! You are an insult to this isle, leave me now! "
msgstr ""

